# ESP32 PWM Parameters on OLED

## Project Overview
This project extends the dual LED PWM fading task by adding an SSD1306 I2C OLED display. The ESP32 controls the brightness of a Red LED and a Blue LED using PWM and displays their current duty cycles and PWM frequency on the OLED screen.

## Task 2: Display PWM Parameters on OLED

### Objectives
- Display the Red LED duty cycle as a percentage.
- Display the Red LED PWM frequency.
- Display the Blue LED duty cycle as a percentage.
- Display the Blue LED PWM frequency.
- Update the OLED values as the LEDs fade.
- Ensure the displayed parameters match the values used in the program.

### Components Used
- ESP32 DevKit
- Red LED
- Blue LED
- 2 × 220Ω resistors
- SSD1306 I2C OLED display (128 × 64)
- Wokwi Simulator
- VS Code with PlatformIO

### Pin Connections

| Component | ESP32 Pin |
|---|---|
| Red LED | GPIO 5 |
| Blue LED | GPIO 23 |
| OLED SDA | GPIO 21 |
| OLED SCL | GPIO 22 |
| OLED VCC | 3.3V |
| OLED GND | GND |

### PWM Configuration

| Parameter | Value |
|---|---|
| PWM Frequency | 5000 Hz |
| PWM Resolution | 8-bit |
| Maximum Duty Value | 255 |
| Duty Cycle Range | 0%–100% |
| Red LED PWM Channel | 0 |
| Blue LED PWM Channel | 1 |
| OLED I2C Address | 0x3C |

### Working Principle
The ESP32 generates PWM signals on two separate channels to control LED brightness. The duty cycle gradually increases from 0 to 255 and then decreases from 255 to 0.

The OLED displays the current duty cycle percentage and configured PWM frequency for each LED. The displayed values refresh continuously as the duty cycles change.

The duty cycle percentage is calculated using:

`Duty Cycle (%) = (Current Duty Value / 255) × 100`

### Expected Output
The OLED displays:
- Red LED duty cycle and frequency.
- Blue LED duty cycle and frequency.
- Continuously updated duty cycle percentages while both LEDs fade in and out.

### Learning Outcomes
- Understanding PWM and duty cycle.
- Controlling multiple LEDs using ESP32 PWM channels.
- Interfacing an SSD1306 OLED using I2C.
- Displaying real-time parameter values.
- Integrating hardware control with an OLED interface.

### Tools and Technologies
- C++
- Arduino Framework
- ESP32
- PlatformIO
- Wokwi Simulator
- Adafruit SSD1306 Library
- Adafruit GFX Library

